**[Optional, finding 6] Paths through names the author chose are ambiguous.**

I checked these, and the builder's paths match `serde_path_to_error`'s rendering, so they are consistent:

- a palette named `a.b` gives `palettes.a.b[0].fill`, which reads like nested keys;
- an empty variant name gives `theme.variants..bg`;
- an empty palette name gives `palettes.[0].fill`;
- an unknown key `""` on a node gives `nodes[0].`.

The error is technically correct but cannot be told apart from a real nested path. Consider quoting `Seg::Name` and unknown keys that are not plain identifiers (`palettes["a.b"][0].fill`). That would also need the parse-time path to be re-rendered from `error.path()` segments rather than its `Display`.

